rcosh}⁡2\\sqrt{3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{{(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{12-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092289 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d3383cb-2322-5ed0-bd5b-631596d72af9" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of Inverse Hyperbolic Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e1275fc-45d5-56e9-921c-419284dfd186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505260} {:answer/id #uuid "64b7ad1d-e8f4-5ece-9cdb-d0b6a18c31ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+6}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505307} {:answer/id #uuid "70ac23c1-c539-56dc-ab99-2f9ae1aa9224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2+\\sqrt{6}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505335} {:answer/id #uuid "c6970587-5e60-5326-ba2f-20db18796990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6-\\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505490} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd92dee-655a-57ac-b2c7-90a821947212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e1275fc-45d5-56e9-921c-419284dfd186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505260} :answer-field/id #uuid "7107c43c-bc1f-5f63-9a1c-c16d62962b34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "854f76b3-c5a6-5b21-803f-68a8249b452b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9601" :question/problem "$$\n\n$\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
